I think that you are misinterpreting their intent.  Delta Air Lines&#x27; President Glen Hauenstein said:<p><pre><code>    &gt; the company&#x27;s AI price-setting technology sets fares by predicting &quot;the amount people are willing to pay for the premium products related to the base fares.&quot;
</code></pre>
It does not affect base fares, only &quot;premium products&quot; (upgrades?).  I always use Google Flights to get high quality search across many airlines.  The industry broadly publishes their base prices in Sabre.  I don&#x27;t see how AI can affect base prices for individual buyers.

You can detect any debugger attached to any browser running V8 with:<p><pre><code>    let cdp = false;
    const orig = Error.prepareStackTrace;
    Error.prepareStackTrace = function () {
      cdp = true;
      return orig;
    };
    console.log(new Error(&#x27;&#x27;));
    &#x2F;&#x2F; cdp === true  → a debugger&#x2F;automation client has the Runtime domain enabled</code></pre>
